 ## Documenting Arguments
 
-{class}`click.argument` does not take a `help` parameter. This follows the Unix Command Line Tools convention of using arguments only for necessary things and documenting them in the command help text
-by name. This should then be done via the docstring.
+{class}`click.argument` takes an optional `help` parameter. Arguments given
+help text are listed in an `Arguments` section of the help page:
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.argument('filename', help='The name of the file to check.')
+    def touch(filename):
+        """Print FILENAME."""
+        click.echo(filename)
+
+.. click:run::
+    invoke(touch, args=['--help'])
+```
+
+Following the Unix Command Line Tools convention, arguments are used only for
+necessary things and are often documented by name in the command help text
+instead. This is done via the docstring.
 
